{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["In the name of El may He strengthen my hand, and His memory establish my majesty. Commentary on the Scroll of Ruth, by Abraham the Sephardi. The utterance of Abraham. Because David is the root of the kingdom of Israel, the lineage of David is recorded in the holy books." "<b>And it came to pass in the days when the judges judged</b>. Some say that שפוט השופטים is a noun [construct], for through them came famine upon the land of Israel. And there is a grammarian who says that it is not a verb but a noun, like חרב שפוט. And it is possible that it is according to its plain sense, for every past or future verb or participle is always derived from the verbal noun, for it is the root." "<b>From Bethlehem Judah</b>: The mem serves both for itself and for what follows it, because a place name is not put in construct state."], :book :ruth, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ruth -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ruth"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:20.644769825Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}